+      "mascotDialogue": "Every arrowhead points just one way here, beta. This particular loop happens to form a cycle, sure — but notice, each edge is still, individually, one-directional. Like a big ensemble scene, everybody's got their own entrance."
+    },
+    "4": {
+      "mascotDialogue": "This, beta, is the single most common directed-graph mistake — treating a one-way arrow like it secretly goes both ways! It does not. The visual only ever draws the direction you actually set, nothing hidden."
